Files written by the C++ writers' own gtests (not hand-made):
- keyframes/{10,30,40}.zip   hydra test_hydra KeyframeSelector.SavesAcceptedKeyframes
- keyframes_multi/{10,10_rear_cam_1,20}.zip
                             hydra test_hydra KeyframeSelector.SensorSuffixForSecondarySensors
                             (sensors "front" and "rear cam/1")
- keyframes_features/10.zip  hydra test_hydra KeyframeSelector.SavesDescriptorsOnlyWhenRequested
                             (save_fields [color, depth, features])
- tracks/12                  khronos test_khronos TrackLogger.WritesTrackAndKeptImages
- tracks/{4,5}               khronos test_khronos TrackLogger.LogsFailedExtraction
- tracks/8                   khronos test_khronos TrackLogger.NonFiniteValuesAreNull
- tracks/sensors.yaml       the sensor record the TrackLogger tests write (the same in all)

The tests delete their temp dirs; they were kept with an LD_PRELOAD shim that makes
std::filesystem::remove_all a no-op (regenerate.sh), run against the
KeyframeSelector and TrackLogger builds of MIT-SPARK/Hydra#199 and MIT-SPARK/Khronos#48.
